 Customer Handoff RAG Tool — Implementation Plan

 Context

 This is for the TASC AI Team home assignment: build a simple internal tool that streamlines a TASC consultant's work, usable by non-technical people. The chosen idea: help a new team quickly get up to speed on an existing customer when they pick up a new project with that customer.

 Two steps, both surfaced in one Streamlit app, no CLI required for end users:
 1. Ingestion tab — a consultant picks a project folder, types the customer's name, and clicks "Run Ingestion Agent." The agent collects everything about the customer from that folder — project files, meeting summaries, public web info — and pushes it into a shared RAG store, tagged with that customer's identity.
 2. Query tab — a new team opens the same app to ask questions about the customer, scoped to just that customer's data.

 Constraints: 2 days total, must be very simple, and the user needs to fully understand and be able to explain every part in a job interview — so no unnecessary complexity or "magic."

 The user will supply a real mock customer folder (project files + meeting summaries) rather than us fabricating a fictional company — so there is no demo-data-authoring step in this plan. The pipeline just needs to work against whatever folder is pointed at it.

 File intake model — UI-driven, not CLI. The ingestion tab has two inputs: a folder picker (path to wherever the project's files already live — any local/shared path, no copying into this repo) and a plain text field for the customer's name. Both inputs persist their last value (written to a small local JSON file, e.g. .last_ingest.json, read back on app start) so re-running for the same customer/folder is a single click. Customer identity is always explicit, typed by the user — never inferred from folder or project names, since a project folder is typically named after the project, not the customer, and guessing would risk silently mixing up customer scoping (the one thing this tool depends on for trust). One folder → one typed customer name → one context_tag.

 When it runs: the natural default to describe in a demo is "at project handoff / end of engagement," but nothing about the design requires that. Because ingestion never resets the collection (pre_delete_collection=False), the same button can be clicked anytime — after a milestone, after a big meeting, mid-project, pointed at a different folder for the same customer — and it only ever adds to that customer's knowledge base. Worth stating explicitly in the interview: "run once at handoff" is the simple story, "can run incrementally, from multiple folders, throughout the project" is true for free, with zero extra engineering.

 Three reference repos already explored, to build on:
 - References/Nivs-RAG/ — minimal FastAPI + LangChain + Postgres/pgvector RAG service (base to build from).
 - References/AI-Agent/ — minimal LangChain tool-calling agent skeleton (create_tool_calling_agent + AgentExecutor + Tool(...) pattern).
 - References/project-template/ — lightweight CLAUDE.md/STATE.md scaffolding conventions (adopt selectively, it's about how we work, not shipped product).                       
